WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:19.021
Hi! Who are you?

2
00:00:19.022 --> 00:00:22.632
I'm a beaver.

3
00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:26.794
Beavers are big rodents.

4
00:00:26.795 --> 00:00:32.817
Rodents have sharp front teeth.

5
00:00:32.818 --> 00:00:36.665
Where do you live?

6
00:00:36.666 --> 00:00:41.249
Beavers live in North America and Europe.

7
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.851
We like to be in fresh water.

8
00:00:45.852 --> 00:00:51.576
Can beavers really cut down trees?

9
00:00:51.577 --> 00:00:56.631
Yes. We use our sharp teeth for that.

10
00:00:56.632 --> 00:01:00.983
We chew through tree trunks.

11
00:01:00.984 --> 00:01:06.893
And then . . . Crash!

12
00:01:06.894 --> 00:01:11.920
What do you do with the trees?

13
00:01:11.921 --> 00:01:15.199
We eat tree bark.

14
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.218
We also use the branches to build things.

15
00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:23.228
What do you build?

16
00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:27.448
We build dams.

17
00:01:27.449 --> 00:01:32.585
Our dams stop streams and make ponds.

18
00:01:32.586 --> 00:01:37.143
We build our homes in those ponds.

19
00:01:37.144 --> 00:01:41.610
What are your homes made of?

20
00:01:41.611 --> 00:01:45.762
They are made of sticks and mud.

21
00:01:45.763 --> 00:01:50.261
Beavers can also dig canals.

22
00:01:50.262 --> 00:01:54.590
We use the canals to carry our branches.

23
00:01:54.591 --> 00:01:59.950
Your tail looks strong.

24
00:01:59.951 --> 00:02:05.932
Our tails help us swim.

25
00:02:05.933 --> 00:02:12.076
We also slap the water with them.

26
00:02:12.077 --> 00:02:20.407
That warns other beavers that enemies are near.

27
00:02:20.408 --> 00:02:22.481
Uh-oh!

28
00:02:22.482 --> 00:02:32.518
An enemy is coming now!

29
00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:38.959
Good-bye, Beaver!
